3.3. Comparative LCA of alternative systems for the production of protein to be used for fishmeal formulation
To determine the potential environmental benefits associated with the production of dried larvae to be used as a source of protein for fishmeal formulation, bioconversion by Hermetia illucens was compared with the production of soybean flour (similarly used for fishmeal formulation) using 1 kg of proteins as FU. Production of 1 kg of protein by dried larvae caused a GWP impact of 2.1 kg CO2 eq, an EU of 15.1 MJ and an LU of 0.05 m2a. Production of 1 kg of protein by soybean caused a GWP impact of 1.7 kg CO2 eq, an EU of 4.1 MJ and an LU of 8.7 m2a. Therefore, using larvae instead of soybean meal caused an increase of GWP and EU (0.4 kg CO2 eq and 11 MJ, respectively), and a
decrease of LU (8.65 m2) (Fig. 5). These results are in accordance with van Zanten et al. (2015), in which, using 1 tonne of larvae meal as a substitute for 0.5 tonnes of soybean meal and 0.5 tonnes of fishmeal, an increase in GWP and EU impacts, and a decrease in LU were highlighted.
